---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';

const id = 'ddpm-training-objective-step';
// α + combining overline, set in the sans font (the serif italic ᾱ reads as a Latin ā).
const AB = 'α̅';
---

<Figure
  id={id}
  title="One training step: draw, jump, predict the noise"
  caption="Each training step draws an image x₀, a random timestep t and a noise ε, jumps straight to xₜ with the closed-form shortcut, asks the network for its estimate εθ(xₜ, t) of the noise, and takes a gradient step on the weighted squared error. The bound-derived objective keeps the weight wₜ; DDPM's unweighted simple loss and the course notebook set wₜ = 1 (and sample t from 1 to T)."
  origin="illustrative"
  pages="44"
>
  <svg class="fig-wide" viewBox="0 0 680 350" role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-w-t ${id}-w-d`}>
    <title id={`${id}-w-t`}>Data flow of one DDPM training step</title>
    <desc id={`${id}-w-d`}>Three input boxes on the left: x0 drawn from the data, t drawn uniformly from 2 to T, and epsilon drawn from N of 0 and I. All three feed a box that computes x t equals square root of alpha bar t times x0 plus square root of 1 minus alpha bar t times epsilon. Its output x t and t go into the blue network box epsilon theta of x t and t. The predicted noise and the true noise epsilon, routed along the bottom, meet in the loss box w t times the squared norm of epsilon minus epsilon theta. The loss feeds a gradient step on theta, which updates the network. A note gives w t equals beta t squared over 2 sigma t squared alpha t times 1 minus alpha bar t, and w t equals 1 for L simple.</desc>

    {/* inputs */}
    <rect class="f-box" x="16" y="28" width="160" height="50" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label f-t-red" x="96" y="50" text-anchor="middle">x₀ ~ data</text>
    <text class="f-note" x="96" y="69" text-anchor="middle">a training image</text>
    <rect class="f-box" x="16" y="116" width="160" height="50" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label" x="96" y="138" text-anchor="middle">t ~ Uniform{'{'}2, …, T{'}'}</text>
    <text class="f-note" x="96" y="157" text-anchor="middle">a random timestep</text>
    <rect class="f-box" x="16" y="204" width="160" height="50" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label" x="96" y="226" text-anchor="middle">ε ~ N(0, I)</text>
    <text class="f-note" x="96" y="245" text-anchor="middle">fresh Gaussian noise</text>

    {/* closed-form jump */}
    <rect class="f-box-soft" x="214" y="94" width="196" height="94" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-note" x="312" y="116" text-anchor="middle">jump straight to xₜ</text>
    <text class="f-label" x="312" y="142" text-anchor="middle">xₜ = √{AB}ₜ x₀</text>
    <text class="f-label" x="312" y="168" text-anchor="middle">+ √(1 − {AB}ₜ) ε</text>
    <path class="f-line" d="M 176 53 Q 196 56 212 112" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <path class="f-line" d="M 176 141 H 211" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <path class="f-line" d="M 176 229 Q 196 226 212 170" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />

    {/* network */}
    <rect class="f-box f-fill-blue" x="446" y="108" width="112" height="66" rx="5" stroke="var(--fig-blue)" />
    <text class="f-math f-t-blue" x="502" y="138" text-anchor="middle">ε<tspan dy="5" font-size="13">θ</tspan><tspan dy="-5">(xₜ, t)</tspan></text>
    <text class="f-note" x="502" y="160" text-anchor="middle">network</text>
    <path class="f-line" d="M 410 141 H 443" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <text class="f-small" x="428" y="131" text-anchor="middle">xₜ, t</text>

    {/* loss */}
    <rect class="f-box" x="420" y="236" width="246" height="52" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-math" x="543" y="268" text-anchor="middle">wₜ <tspan font-style="normal">‖</tspan>ε − ε<tspan dy="5" font-size="13">θ</tspan><tspan dy="-5">(xₜ, t)</tspan><tspan font-style="normal">‖</tspan>²</text>
    <path class="f-line f-blue" d="M 502 174 V 233" marker-end="url(#f-arrow-blue)" />
    <text class="f-small f-t-blue" x="494" y="210" text-anchor="end">predicted noise</text>
    <path class="f-line f-red" d="M 96 254 V 274 H 417" marker-end="url(#f-arrow-red)" />
    <text class="f-small f-t-red" x="300" y="266" text-anchor="middle">true noise ε</text>

    {/* gradient step and update */}
    <rect class="f-box" x="588" y="108" width="84" height="66" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label" x="630" y="136" text-anchor="middle">gradient</text>
    <text class="f-label" x="630" y="156" text-anchor="middle">step</text>
    <path class="f-line" d="M 630 236 V 177" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <path class="f-line f-dash" d="M 630 108 Q 630 66 566 66 Q 514 66 509 105" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <text class="f-label" x="570" y="56" text-anchor="middle">update θ</text>

    <text class="f-small" x="543" y="314" text-anchor="middle">from the bound: wₜ = βₜ² / (2σₜ² αₜ (1 − {AB}ₜ))</text>
    <text class="f-small f-t-muted" x="543" y="334" text-anchor="middle">L<tspan dy="4" font-size="10">simple</tspan><tspan dy="-4"> and the notebook: wₜ = 1</tspan></text>
  </svg>

  <svg class="fig-narrow" viewBox="0 0 360 580" role="img" aria-labelledby={`${id}-n-t ${id}-n-d`}>
    <title id={`${id}-n-t`}>Data flow of one DDPM training step</title>
    <desc id={`${id}-n-d`}>Top: three input boxes, x0 from the data, t uniform from 2 to T, epsilon from N of 0 and I. They feed the box x t equals square root of alpha bar t times x0 plus square root of 1 minus alpha bar t times epsilon, which feeds the blue network epsilon theta of x t and t. The predicted noise and the true noise epsilon, routed down the right side, meet in the loss box w t times the squared norm of epsilon minus epsilon theta, which feeds a gradient step that updates the network. Notes give the weight from the bound and w t equals 1 for L simple.</desc>

    <rect class="f-box" x="6" y="14" width="108" height="56" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label f-t-red" x="60" y="38" text-anchor="middle">x₀ ~ data</text>
    <text class="f-note" x="60" y="58" text-anchor="middle">image</text>
    <rect class="f-box" x="126" y="14" width="108" height="56" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label" x="180" y="38" text-anchor="middle">t ~ U{'{'}2…T{'}'}</text>
    <text class="f-note" x="180" y="58" text-anchor="middle">timestep</text>
    <rect class="f-box" x="246" y="14" width="108" height="56" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label" x="300" y="38" text-anchor="middle">ε ~ N(0, I)</text>
    <text class="f-note" x="300" y="58" text-anchor="middle">noise</text>

    <rect class="f-box-soft" x="50" y="112" width="260" height="66" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-note" x="180" y="134" text-anchor="middle">jump straight to xₜ</text>
    <text class="f-label" x="180" y="162" text-anchor="middle">xₜ = √{AB}ₜ x₀ + √(1 − {AB}ₜ) ε</text>
    <path class="f-line" d="M 60 70 L 92 109" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <path class="f-line" d="M 180 70 V 109" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <path class="f-line" d="M 300 70 L 268 109" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />

    <rect class="f-box f-fill-blue" x="110" y="222" width="140" height="62" rx="5" stroke="var(--fig-blue)" />
    <text class="f-math f-t-blue" x="180" y="250" text-anchor="middle">ε<tspan dy="5" font-size="13">θ</tspan><tspan dy="-5">(xₜ, t)</tspan></text>
    <text class="f-note" x="180" y="272" text-anchor="middle">network</text>
    <path class="f-line" d="M 180 178 V 219" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <text class="f-small" x="190" y="204">xₜ, t</text>

    <rect class="f-box" x="70" y="330" width="250" height="52" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-math" x="195" y="362" text-anchor="middle">wₜ <tspan font-style="normal">‖</tspan>ε − ε<tspan dy="5" font-size="13">θ</tspan><tspan dy="-5">(xₜ, t)</tspan><tspan font-style="normal">‖</tspan>²</text>
    <path class="f-line f-blue" d="M 180 284 V 327" marker-end="url(#f-arrow-blue)" />
    <text class="f-small f-t-blue" x="190" y="312">predicted noise</text>
    <path class="f-line f-red" d="M 340 70 V 346 Q 340 356 330 356 H 323" marker-end="url(#f-arrow-red)" />
    <text class="f-small f-t-red" x="332" y="240" text-anchor="end">true</text>
    <text class="f-small f-t-red" x="332" y="256" text-anchor="end">noise ε</text>

    <rect class="f-box" x="120" y="428" width="120" height="48" rx="5" />
    <text class="f-label" x="180" y="457" text-anchor="middle">gradient step</text>
    <path class="f-line" d="M 180 382 V 425" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <path class="f-line f-dash" d="M 120 452 C 30 452 30 253 107 253" marker-end="url(#f-arrow)" />
    <text class="f-label" transform="translate(22 352) rotate(-90)" text-anchor="middle">update θ</text>

    <text class="f-small" x="180" y="516" text-anchor="middle">from the bound: wₜ = βₜ² / (2σₜ² αₜ (1 − {AB}ₜ))</text>
    <text class="f-small f-t-muted" x="180" y="538" text-anchor="middle">L<tspan dy="4" font-size="10">simple</tspan><tspan dy="-4"> and the notebook: wₜ = 1</tspan></text>
  </svg>
</Figure>
